    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHallo, your work is greatly appreciated.\n\n### Proposal\n\nI wonder if there is a reason why `MiniAi.move_cursor` doesn't add new entries for the jumplist. My knowledge of lua and neovim is limited and probably I missed something, but for example like this:\n```lua\n-- mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua\n-- ...\nMiniAi.move_cursor = function(side, ai_type, id, opts)\n  -- ...\n  vim.cmd(\"normal! m'\")\n  -- Move cursor and open enough folds\n  vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { pos.line, pos.col - 1 })\n  vim.cmd('normal! zv')\n  vim.cmd(\"normal! m'\")\nend\n-- ...\n```\n\n### related issues\nI tried to search the issues, but couldn't find duplicate for the functionality I'm looking for.\n- [mini.ai issue](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/149) - I couldn't fully grasp the problem.",
