            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> I wonder if there is a reason why `MiniAi.move_cursor` doesn't add new entries for the jumplist.\n\nThere is no one *particular* reason, but there are several:\n- Not every movement adds position to jumplist. See `:h jump-motions`. So deciding when movement adds to jump list and when not is a bit ambiguous. The best guess is to add if the movement changes line, but that is still no one-to-one how it is done for built-in movements (`w` / `b` / `e` can change line, but they don't add to jumplist).\n- The 'mini.ai' is mostly about selecting textobjects and not moving cursor. So this was just glossed over.\n\nI'll think a bit more about this.",
